    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d393">

                <pb facs="0535" n="523" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg523"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 PW/5–2546: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-05-25T14:00:00-04:00">May 25, 1946—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>974. For your info in connection visit Pauley to
                    northern Korea following received from Pauley today: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Please inform interested parties that Moscow’s 41,<anchor n="49"
                                xml:id="d393-f1"/> as I understand it, denies my mission access as
                            suggested in my letter of May 20 <pb facs="0536" n="524" xml:id="pg524"
                            /> to Chistiakov setting forth a full itinerary and placed me in a
                            position of either not going north of the 38 parallel, or going with a
                            bandage over my eyes.</p>
                        <p>I propose now to do the latter, but continue to press for full plan. In
                            the meantime, will establish a base at Mukden for Manchuria operation,
                            maintaining a minimum sized base in Seoul.”<anchor n="50"
                                xml:id="d393-f2"/></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d393-f1" n="49" xml:id="d393-f1-content">
                <p>See last sentence of telegram 1609, May 22, noon, from Moscow, <ref
                        target="#pg520">p. 520</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d393-f2" n="50" xml:id="d393-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 975, May 25, 4 p.m., to Moscow, the Department reported Mr. Pauley’s
                    latest message offering further limitations on his proposed visit to north Korea
                    in connection with a new request to the Soviet Foreign Office (740.00119
                    P.W./5–2546).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
